  "evidence": "The text explicitly opens with “Labour’s 2024 manifesto” and is structured around Labour’s “five national missions.” It names signature Labour policies and language from 2024: Great British Energy (£8.3bn), a National Wealth Fund (£7.3bn), Warm Homes Plan (£6.6bn), “Make Brexit work” (no single market/customs union/FoM), the New Deal for Working People (zero‑hours/fire‑and‑rehire), a cap on corporation tax at 25%, no rises in NI/Income Tax/VAT, abolishing non‑dom status, ‘First steps for change’ (six first steps: NHS waits, Border Security Command, Great British Energy, antisocial behaviour, 6,500 teachers, economic stability).",
  "confidence": "high",
  "identification": "A condensed summary of the UK Labour Party’s 2024 General Election manifesto—‘Change: Labour Party Manifesto 2024’—and its accompanying ‘Six First Steps for Change’ pledge card, as published by the Labour Party in June 2024."
}
